Do not re-escape a URL that is already escaped, on macOS.

JUCE 8.0.14's WebKit/WKWebView backend percent-encodes every string handed to
goToURL() before building the request, with URLQueryAllowedCharacterSet. That
set does not contain '%', so an escape already in the string is escaped again:
"%3A" becomes "%253A", and the server that decodes it once is handed the literal
text "https%3A%2F%2F..." rather than the URL it stands for.

Any correctly-built query string is affected. Plectrify hit it on the TONE3000
OAuth flow, where redirect_uri is a URL inside a query parameter and so must be
escaped: TONE3000 answered "redirect_uri must be a valid URL", quoting our
escapes back. It equally mangles any escaped parameter in a page the user
navigates to inside that window.

The encoding is there to rescue a string that is not a valid URL (a raw space,
say), so keep it for exactly that case: try the string as given first, and only
escape when NSURL rejects it. A valid URL then reaches WebKit untouched.

diff --git a/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_mac.mm b/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_mac.mm
--- a/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_mac.mm
+++ b/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_mac.mm
@@ -61,7 +61,13 @@
 {
     NSString* urlString = juceStringToNS (url);
 
-     urlString = [urlString stringByAddingPercentEncodingWithAllowedCharacters: [NSCharacterSet URLQueryAllowedCharacterSet]];
+     // PLECTRIFY_NO_DOUBLE_ESCAPE_URL: only escape a string that is not already
+     // a valid URL. URLQueryAllowedCharacterSet excludes '%', so escaping
+     // unconditionally turns every existing escape into a literal one - a
+     // redirect_uri of "https%3A%2F%2Fhost%2Fpath" is delivered to the server as
+     // that text rather than as the URL it encodes.
+     if ([NSURL URLWithString: urlString] == nil)
+         urlString = [urlString stringByAddingPercentEncodingWithAllowedCharacters: [NSCharacterSet URLQueryAllowedCharacterSet]];
 
      if (NSURL* nsURL = [NSURL URLWithString: urlString])
      {
